If $T_{\rm chosen}\geq T_f$, there is no throughput payback. For $n$ queries per batch, batch time is $T=1000n/Q$ milliseconds.
For varying choices, convexity gives $1/\mathbb E[Q]\leq\mathbb E[1/Q]$: inverse mean QPS understates mean time. Boundaries/direct checks follow \cref{sec:a-budget-contract,sec:7-stream-cost}.
Campaign estimates are in \cref{tab:7-budget-cost}.

